<h2 id="our-experience">🏥 Our Experience Testing Esignly</h2>

Our team has worked across dozens of aesthetics practices — from single-injector suites to multi-location med spa groups — evaluating how software holds up under real clinic conditions. We tested Esignly over a six-week period, building out a full library of aesthetics consent forms including neurotoxin, dermal filler, PRP, microneedling, laser hair removal, and chemical peel consents.

Here is what stood out immediately: setup is genuinely fast. We had a branded neurotoxin consent form live and ready for client signing within 22 minutes of creating an account. The drag-and-drop form builder is intuitive — you upload a PDF or build from a blank canvas, drop in signature fields, initials fields, date stamps, and checkboxes, and you are done.

We also ran the client-facing flow from a tablet in "kiosk mode," which is how most front desks will use this. Clients see a clean, professional interface. They read, sign, and submit — and the signed document lands in your dashboard instantly with a timestamp and IP log.

Where we noticed friction: there is no direct integration with common aesthetics platforms like <a href="https://medspaoperator.io/reviews/jane-app">Jane App</a> or <a href="https://medspaoperator.io/reviews/boulevard">Boulevard</a>. You will manage Esignly as a standalone tool, which means manually reconciling signed consents with your appointment records. For high-volume practices processing 50+ clients per day, that gap matters. For a boutique clinic doing 15-20 treatments per day, it is a manageable workflow.

<div class="callout-blue">
  <strong>💡 Tip:</strong> Build a naming convention for your consent documents from day one — include the client's name, treatment type, and date in the file name. Esignly's search and filter tools work well when your documents are consistently named.
</div>

---

<h2 id="key-features">⚙️ Key Features for Aesthetics Clinics</h2>

<h3>Template Library and Custom Form Builder</h3>

Esignly ships with 300+ pre-built templates across industries. The healthcare-adjacent templates are a starting point, not a finish line — you will want to replace or heavily customize them with your clinic's specific consent language, liability waivers, and treatment disclosures. The good news is the custom builder makes this straightforward. You can import your existing Word or PDF consent forms and layer on signature fields in minutes.

<h3>In-Clinic Kiosk Mode</h3>

One of the most practical features for aesthetics operators. Kiosk mode locks the app to your consent form on an iPad or tablet, clients complete and sign, and the session resets for the next client. No staff handling required beyond handing over the device. This is the feature most of our team's clinic contacts specifically asked about, and Esignly delivers it cleanly.

<h3>SMS and Email Signature Requests</h3>

Pre-appointment consent collection is the gold standard for client experience and appointment efficiency. Esignly lets you send a signature request link via email or SMS before the client arrives. For practices that want clients walking in already consented and ready to be treated, this is a significant time-saver. We tested delivery speed — SMS links arrived within 10 seconds consistently.

<h3>Audit Trail and Document Storage</h3>

Every signed document includes a timestamped audit trail — IP address, signing time, email verification, and device information. This is legally relevant for consent documentation. Esignly stores all documents in encrypted cloud storage with role-based access controls. The audit trail satisfies most state-level consent documentation requirements, though you should confirm specifics with your healthcare attorney for your jurisdiction.

<div class="callout-orange">
  <strong>⚠️ Warning:</strong> Esignly does not carry a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) on its standard plans. If your consent forms capture Protected Health Information (PHI) as defined under HIPAA, you need to either upgrade to an enterprise arrangement with a BAA in place or evaluate whether the data captured falls within HIPAA scope for your practice. Consult your compliance advisor before going live.
</div>

<h3>Multi-User Team Access</h3>

You can add team members with role-based permissions — useful for clinics with front desk staff handling document sends and managers needing reporting access. The permissions structure is not granular enough for complex organizational hierarchies, but it covers the basic separation of front-desk, injector, and admin roles.

<h3>Branding and White-Label Customization</h3>

Upload your clinic logo, set brand colors, and customize the email templates clients receive. The branded experience matters for aesthetics practices where client trust and visual consistency drive retention. Esignly's branding tools hit the essentials without overcomplicating the setup.

<h3>Integrations via Zapier</h3>

Esignly connects to 1,000+ apps through Zapier, which is how you bridge the gap with your booking or practice management system. We built a working Zap that triggered a consent form send automatically when a new appointment was created in a test Google Calendar — functional, though it requires Zapier familiarity and an additional subscription. Native aesthetics integrations would be a meaningful upgrade to the product.

