<h2 id="final-verdict">🏁 Final Verdict</h2>

Esignly earns its place in the aesthetics operator's toolkit as a clean, affordable, and genuinely functional solution for digital consent form collection. It is not trying to be your EMR, your booking system, or your HIPAA compliance officer — and that focus shows in how well the core eSignature workflow actually performs.

The absence of native aesthetics integrations and the BAA complexity on standard plans are real limitations that matter depending on your practice size and compliance posture. But for the solo injector or boutique studio that currently relies on paper consent forms — or a generic Google Form that provides no real audit trail — Esignly is a meaningful upgrade at a price that justifies the switch immediately.

Our team's honest recommendation: sign up for the free trial, build your three most-used consent forms (neurotoxin, filler, and one energy device or chemical peel consent), run your front desk through the tablet kiosk flow, and assess whether the manual reconciliation with your booking system is tolerable for your volume. For most boutique practices, it will be.

